# Tuning applied to IDENTITY=own only.
#
# This file is appended to arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig right before the
# build generates its .config, so these are the last word on each symbol. It is
# NOT applied to `repro`, because repro has to stay an exact copy of the phone's
# kernel; that is what makes a bad boot mean "our change" and not "our pipeline".
#
# Every line here is also what configs/verify-allow.txt is allowed to forgive,
# by construction: scripts/20-verify.sh reads this file and accepts exactly
# these symbols. A diff outside this list still fails the build.
#
# One entry per reason. If a knob cannot say why it is here, it does not belong.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. KernelAddressSanitizer is off.
#
# The phone's config has CONFIG_KASAN=y with CONFIG_KASAN_HW_TAGS=y, i.e. memory
# tagging instrumentation active in a daily driver. It is a debugging feature:
# it costs CPU on every allocation, costs memory for tags/redzones, and buys
# nothing on a phone that is not being fuzzed. This is the single largest
# runtime cost in the current config.
#
# This does not weaken CFI, pointer authentication or BTI: those stay.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_KASAN is not set

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. zram, i.e. compressed swap in RAM.
#
# The tree has drivers/block/zram and mm/zsmalloc, but they were not built, so
# this kernel has no swap at all: when memory runs out, Android kills apps
# instead of compressing cold pages. On 8-12 GB that is wasted headroom, and
# every kill means a cold app start later, which costs battery.
#
# Default compressor stays lzo-rle (lowest CPU cost per byte). zstd compresses
# better but burns more CPU; that trade is worth testing later, not assuming.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_ZRAM=y
# Selected by ZRAM, but named explicitly: the verifier tolerates exactly the
# symbols listed here, and a side effect nobody wrote down is a side effect
# nobody agreed to.
CONFIG_ZSMALLOC=y
# zram's lzo-rle compressor pulls this in. First build failed verification
# precisely because it was not written here, which is the mechanism working.
CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZO=y

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Debug symbols are not built.
#
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO with DWARF4 is ~1 GB of vmlinux nobody ships. It does not
# change the Image at all, it only makes every build slower and every artifact
# bigger. Turning it off is free.
#
# The two lines after it are not settings, they are the symbols that stop
# existing once DEBUG_INFO is off. They are listed so the verifier's record of
# this build is complete: it tolerates a change only if the change is written
# here, and "the config dropped an option because its parent went away" is still
# a change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO is not set
# CONFIG_GDB_SCRIPTS is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_EFI is not set
